WEBVTT

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:57.690
You got it?

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.340
I was hoping for your...

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.763
... For your wisdom, General.

00:02:13.907 --> 00:02:14.934
Give it to me.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:45.520
Fuck.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:46.480
Finally.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.830
Eyes on the target.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:09.820
Good.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.060
Agent Hooper?

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.520
Yes, mother.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.480
Good position?

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.867
The sexist position of the blonde
girl in the short red dress and the

00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:19.800
knee-high boots at the bar was
next to no purpose on this mission.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:20.900
Yeah?

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.900
Agent Becky Hooper, reporting for duty.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.000
A simple affirmative would have sufficed.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.240
For what it's worth,
I think you were good in red.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.200
You're stupid, and I hate you.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.840
Just give him the glass, Becky.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.460
I'd say wish me luck,
but we both know I don't need it.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.280
All right, remember.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.003
We need three
minutes to download the

00:03:44.045 --> 00:03:46.040
contents of the
computer in that briefcase.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.320
Mr. Sterling.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.300
I'm afraid my mom skipped that lesson.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:03:59.640
So charming.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.620
Four percent of the total.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.180
More this time.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.940
Tell me about the Raven.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.500
Something wrong?

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.140
Twenty-five percent, my dear.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.589
You didn't actually think
you could show the Iranians

00:04:35.631 --> 00:04:38.880
the next generation of Rome
and keep it quiet, did you?

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:39.660
The Raven is the next generation.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:40.600
It's not for sale.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.340
Everything is for sale, Mr. Hooper.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.240
Backup stopped.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.260
What happened?

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.240
They took the glass.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:04:59.940
What do you mean, they took the glass?

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.500
I mean, the waitress took the glass.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.000
The glass with the
remote hard drive in it.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.240
The glass critical to the mission.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:07.720
All right.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.260
We're on our way to plan B.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.080
Copy that.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.140
Excuse me?

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.740
I don't like being ambushed, Mr. Pierce.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:15.520
This meeting is over.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.240
Give him the codes.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:19.900
I don't like being ambushed.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.180
What's this?

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.500
A sign of good faith.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:28.360
The codes.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.140
A single satellite
controlled by the Saudis.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.940
Encrypted from top to bottom.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:34.680
Untraceable.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.160
And you suspect this will make me tall?

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:43.700
What could be of
more value to Golshiri

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:47.240
than the power to
control his enemy's skies?

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.380
And for you to be the
one to bring it to him.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:10.680
Well, I don't know.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.600
I'll teach you a little something
I learned a long time ago.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.674
In this line of work,
you'd be wise never to accept

00:06:17.716 --> 00:06:21.000
drinks from a random
woman dressed like that.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:25.500
Drink is spiked.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.120
Good.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.120
For a B, you really need
to take a sip of that drink.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.160
What do you say?

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.100
The raven or the rest of the coat?

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.620
Sounds like an arrangement
worth drinking to.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:40.040
As I said, the raven is not for sale.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.640
Goodbye, Mr. Pierce.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:43.760
Greetings.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.480
I say this to Montana...

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.820
Cooper, do not say it.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.240
Time for plan C.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.240
Becky?

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.420
There is no plan C.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:53.880
Becky?

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:55.360
Oh, and another thing.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:59.300
The next time your employer wants to do
business, he should contact me directly.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.960
You're not so pretty close up.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:06.940
Becky?

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.680
We're going to need that briefcase.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.760
And who is it you think you are?

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.920
I'm the one you didn't expect.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:14.800
Fuck!

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:26.780
Two years ago, you somehow
convinced me that recruiting a 16-year

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.400
-old girl with anger management
issues was a good idea.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:34.159
In that time, she abused the
agency's reach and blew a man up.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.869
She obliterated several of
her fellow agents, costing

00:08:38.911 --> 00:08:41.700
us copious amounts in
facial reconstruction surgeries.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:42.620
Oh, fuck!

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:44.080
Jesus Christ, Becky!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:45.960
This is a fucking training exercise!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.300
She went rogue on the first,
second, and now third mission.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:52.540
Time for plan C.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.800
Time for plan C!

00:08:58.880 --> 00:08:59.640
Time for plan C.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.166
No matter how many times
the CIA suspends her, or

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.780
how many times the CIA
sends her to therapy sessions,

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:11.840
nothing changes.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:13.220
Nothing.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:14.500
Director?

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.960
Do you think this is a conversation
that we should be having in private?

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:19.500
Why?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.500
Has it worked out so
well the last 12 times?

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.600
Sterling was our best
shot at accessing the intel.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:27.140
Tied to one of the biggest
arms dealers out of Europe.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.100
And I got you a laptop, didn't I?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.200
No, Agent Hooper.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.080
You destroyed it when it was too late.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:36.320
I know.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:37.200
Yeah.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:39.700
Oops.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:41.160
Yeah.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:42.320
Oops.

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:46.480
If you have a problem with my methods,
then why the hell am I still here?

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:48.460
Your methods?

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:49.100
Mm.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.340
Oh, that's very good.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:51.960
Hooper, you're excused.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:52.740
Rigby, you too.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.150
Return to New York where
you'll await further instruction on

00:09:57.192 --> 00:09:59.840
whether or not you'll be seeking
employment at your local boutique.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.620
Oh, ma'am, with all due respect,
I've been- Get the fuck out of my office!

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:03.100
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:16.600
Montana, that girl is a danger
to herself and her comrades.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.660
She cares more about these
missions than any other agent we have.

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:20.740
Oh, I ain't picking up on that.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:21.980
She's a fighter.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.000
No, she's a psychopath.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:37.850
The CIA relocated me
to New York after training.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.310
Smells like shit.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:42.530
It's loud as hell.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.330
The people are jackasses.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.010
I love everything about it.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:57.700
Yeah.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:10:58.860
A landline.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.200
Go work for the CIA for two years.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.140
You ditch your cell phone, too.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:03.680
Delivery.

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:10.850
The past.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:12.710
I was better off alone.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.469
It took me too long to
realize that I was the angel

00:11:16.511 --> 00:11:18.970
of death in the lives of
anyone I cared about.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:23.050
But I refused to let anything
bad happen to Diego.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.510
So I found him a new home.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:32.950
Sometimes, it's all just too much.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.010
And everything goes dark.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.080
I can't read without a regret.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:46.660
Uh-oh.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.960
I don't have to go to school.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:50.500
I don't have to go to school.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.497
When I first joined the CIA,
they put me

00:12:08.539 --> 00:12:11.340
through all these tests
and psych evaluations.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.300
It felt like I was under a microscope.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.340
State your full name, age, place of birth.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.360
I don't even have that on file from
like the last five times we did this.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:23.880
Do you make new friends easily?

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:25.320
I don't know.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:26.440
Never tried.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:29.400
How old were you when
you got into your first fight?

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:30.440
Nine.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.140
I broke the kid's face.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:35.120
They asked me if I'd
always been so unhappy.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:36.920
So angry.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.000
How did you feel when your father died?

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:42.760
Becky?

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.000
I was super.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:46.320
It was great.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:47.060
What a fun time.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:48.680
What does it matter?

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:50.120
Shit happens.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:08.680
This is Fox.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.400
Sir, this is worse than we thought.

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:11.860
Well, Helm's lying to me.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:12.860
Maybe he suspects something.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.040
I don't know.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.700
But, sir,
the Forsyte's just the fucking beginning.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.560
Russell, everything okay?

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:22.900
Get out of the car.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.200
I was just calling a friend.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.140
I've picked up a new hobby
since joining the agency.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:39.520
Swords.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:42.800
Like knives, but bigger.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.340
Hey, you've gotten better.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:50.880
Can you improvise?

00:13:56.100 --> 00:14:05.630
How was that?

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.630
Come on.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:13.670
Hooper.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.680
The director's here to see you.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:23.520
Not you, Rigby.

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:24.180
Just Hooper.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.910
I'll go quietly,
but I'm keeping the apartment.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:37.130
And the suits.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:37.990
Shut up and listen.

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:41.866
Now, four years ago,
you had the misfortune of crossing paths

00:14:41.908 --> 00:14:45.950
with a group of escaped convicts
led by this man, Dominic Lewis.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.750
They were looking for a key
under your family's lake house.

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:56.050
Well, it's about fucking time.

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:00.073
Our best guess is that the
key had been hidden decades

00:15:00.115 --> 00:15:03.410
earlier by the Helm's former owner,
a man named Joseph Alpert.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.410
Real name?

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:05.950
Johan Roos.

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:08.810
Now, Johan, good old-fashioned Nazi.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.090
One of his favorites, actually.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.890
A leading bioengineer in the
development of nerve agents.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:18.910
Now, by 1946, he became a first-round
draft pick in Operation Paperclip.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:23.010
He enjoyed the American dream for
a few decades before dying in 1987.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:26.190
Survived by his grandson, Wilhelm Roos.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:30.090
Well, it appears he's proven
to be quite the problem child.

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:34.010
We now know he's been the mastermind
behind Dominic Lewis' jailbreak.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:38.190
Step one in a multi-pronged
plan to usher in the Fourth Reich.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:43.850
Step two was to obtain the key, which
would lead as a roadmap to step three.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:46.230
These are UTM coordinates.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.102
They lead to a forest in Poland,
the site of Hitler's

00:15:49.144 --> 00:15:51.470
military headquarters
during the Second World War.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.190
A place more commonly known as...

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.330
the Wolf's Lair.

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:02.213
You'll imagine our surprise when Wilhelm
here relocates his family there, joined

00:16:02.255 --> 00:16:06.930
by his right-hand, Russell Wagner,
and his associate, Dr. Friedrich Metzger.

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:11.170
Now, thermal imagery indicates that there
is something going on underneath the lair.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:14.570
How did Wilhelm know where
to go if he doesn't have the key?

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.650
Well, he does have the key.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:18.710
What?

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:19.330
How?

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:20.910
We gave it to him.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:25.010
Okay, so you gave the man
trying to usher in the Fourth Reich

00:16:25.052 --> 00:16:28.470
the very thing he may need in
order to usher in the Fourth Reich.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.110
Sometimes national security
requires dining with the devil.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.390
We had an asset on the inside,
Agent Jeffrey Fox.

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.250
We received a distress call from him.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:39.710
We believe it's been made.

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:42.090
Okay,
so you want me to go on a rescue mission?

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.510
They have identified Fox as an agent.

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.550
There is no one left to rescue.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:51.670
Agent Hooper, you will travel to
Poland at 0900 hours tomorrow.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.730
Once there,
you'll pick up where Agent Fox left off.

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:56.876
The Roos family
lives on the site of the

00:16:56.918 --> 00:16:58.770
lair soon,
which is where you'll be staying.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:01.230
So Hitler's men care, huh?

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.849
In a gift shop, in case you need a hat.

00:17:03.849 --> 00:17:06.565
Collect what intel you
can on what it is Willem

00:17:06.607 --> 00:17:09.190
is doing beneath that
bunker and report back.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:10.390
That's it.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.150
In other words, try not to kill anyone.

00:17:13.349 --> 00:17:15.730
And Agent, the Noblemen
aren't the only terror organization

00:17:15.772 --> 00:17:17.790
in the world trying to get
through the government.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.650
Extremist groups are rising
up all around the globe.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:25.170
But Roos, he is one of the most
terrible and dangerous of them all.

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:29.270
So I ask him, are you up for this?

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:33.640
Nazi.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:35.780
Halt!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:47.680
For 80 years, we have been plagued
by the ignorant ways of our enemies.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:53.753
Forced to hide among them,
to feign unity, to

00:17:53.795 --> 00:17:58.900
stand by and suffer
whilst bearing the burden of

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:00.300
a superior way.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:08.060
We know it takes only one man to bring
the Almighty's light into the darkness.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:12.958
And thanks to you,
and to our fellows around the world

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:17.400
who watch and wait for our command,
we stand here

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:23.740
today on this hallowed
ground at the edge of greatness.

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:28.520
The light is coming!

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:29.220
Yeah!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:45.931
Just as one man can
choose to lead us to victory,

00:18:45.973 --> 00:18:49.980
so too can one choose
to bring our demise.

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:55.520
As made his choice.

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:07.780
And in the words of our Fuhrer,
if men wish to live, then

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.920
they are forced to kill others.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.720
Men can stand in our way.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:40.909
Your Alexis Taylor, American college
student, getting your world history degree

00:19:40.951 --> 00:19:44.240
from Columbia, but you're making your
way through Europe between semesters.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.140
A car will be waiting
for you when you land.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.230
I guess I could stab someone with this.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.830
It's inspired by Havana syndrome.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:55.110
You press the top.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.750
Don't actually press the top.

00:19:57.310 --> 00:20:00.830
It emits a frequency that
disorients anyone with an earshot.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:02.270
And what happens to me?

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:06.050
When pressed, a small prick
will inject a substance I know.

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:09.410
Temporarily relax your cochlear nerve.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:12.230
That hearing loss will make
you immune to the effects.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.250
Ah, Pontianak!

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.290
It's a blow dart.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:19.050
The muzzle's on the bottom.

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:22.154
The projectile is a
splinter that is coated in an

00:20:22.196 --> 00:20:24.610
engineered compound
that resembles nitroglycerin.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:27.283
It pierces the skin,
interacts with the iron in the

00:20:27.325 --> 00:20:29.590
blood,
and reaches critical mass within moments.

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:30.670
English.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.770
Turn other person into all.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.410
Okay, seriously, Mom?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.480
Yeah, alright, that's lapsed.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:43.740
Yeah.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:46.320
Not normally our style,
but I thought you'd like it.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:48.360
Eye drops.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:49.080
Poison.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:50.800
Baby grenade launcher.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:51.840
Sub-vocal detector.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:52.700
Tiny flashlight.

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:54.080
Signal jammer.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.200
And tiny flashlight.

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:58.880
Becky?

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:02.760
This is your last chance.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:05.280
Baker's only giving you one more shot.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:08.180
Oh, well, I'll be sure to send her thank
you chocolates when I start giving up.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:09.220
Can you cut the shit?

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:10.900
We get it.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.900
The world burned you.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:12.920
You're gonna burn the world.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.320
This is a very tired act.

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.696
Oh, this is the part where
you tell me you were angry

00:21:16.738 --> 00:21:19.000
too once and found a
better life on the other side?

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:20.060
No.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:24.080
This is the part where I tell you that
the world doesn't revolve around you.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:27.560
What happened to you happened.

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.620
The least interesting thing about you.

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:32.760
Stop letting it define you.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.700
Come to see me off?

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:48.400
For a solo mission and all?

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:51.480
Try not to die.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:52.500
Aw.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:53.900
You'd miss me?

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:54.480
Nope.

00:21:55.340 --> 00:21:57.760
Just don't feel like flying all the
way to Poland to pick up a coffin.

00:21:58.840 --> 00:21:59.360
Charming.

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:10.610
You should find out what these
fuckers are up to, couldn't you?

00:22:56.320 --> 00:22:59.326
It took all of two seconds
for me to figure out

00:22:59.368 --> 00:23:02.540
that this place was my
own personal hell on earth.

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:12.440
Or the life-size
cardboard cutout of Hitler.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:18.440
Metame.

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:19.440
Metame.

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:20.560
How can I help you?

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:22.080
My name is Alexis Taylor.

00:23:22.220 --> 00:23:24.040
I believe I have a
reservation for one night.

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.300
Luisa!

00:23:27.320 --> 00:23:27.980
Metame.

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:28.700
Metame.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:29.700
Alexis Taylor.

00:23:30.020 --> 00:23:32.000
She believes she has a
reservation for one night.

00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:33.620
I see.

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:39.150
Mother!

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:44.860
Metame.

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:45.980
Metame.

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:47.520
Alexis Taylor.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:49.940
She believes she has a
reservation for one night.

00:23:50.140 --> 00:23:50.880
Of course.

00:24:04.800 --> 00:24:06.060
Let us see.

00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:12.980
Here we are.

00:24:14.520 --> 00:24:16.720
And will anyone be joining you?

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:19.640
No, no, it's just me.

00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:23.840
Well then.

00:24:31.260 --> 00:24:33.460
Welcome to the Wolf's Lair.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:36.920
Any questions you may have
can be directed to Otto here.

00:24:37.260 --> 00:24:42.447
Each night we provide
dinner for the guests at seven

00:24:42.489 --> 00:24:47.420
p.m. sharp and curfew is
nine p.m. to six a.m. Um,

00:24:47.420 --> 00:24:48.040
curfew?

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:49.960
For the safety of our guests.

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:54.020
Was this forest for once
littered with land mines?

00:24:54.700 --> 00:24:55.460
Unlikely, sir.

00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:58.715
It left,
but we wouldn't want a pretty thing like

00:24:58.757 --> 00:25:01.780
you wandering about
and helping us to find out.

00:25:02.580 --> 00:25:03.200
Right.

00:25:06.220 --> 00:25:11.220
Dropped my stuff off.

00:25:11.220 --> 00:25:14.620
I made my way to the
pink tourist attraction.

00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:23.360
Ah, the Wolf's Lair.

00:25:24.520 --> 00:25:25.800
Nazi wonderland.

00:25:26.640 --> 00:25:29.640
You can smell the desperation
for world domination in the air.

00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:32.060
And it smelled faintly of cabbage.

00:25:33.860 --> 00:25:35.220
Dr. Adams with the General.

00:25:38.220 --> 00:25:45.800
Well, well.

00:25:46.360 --> 00:25:47.680
Who do we have here?

00:25:52.550 --> 00:25:53.590
Family?

00:25:54.170 --> 00:25:54.310
Check.

00:25:54.650 --> 00:25:55.330
Friends?

00:25:55.810 --> 00:25:56.330
Check.

00:25:56.870 --> 00:25:58.570
Now where's Wilhelm?

00:26:02.790 --> 00:26:04.770
Wait, who's this?

00:26:05.010 --> 00:26:05.590
Who are you?

00:26:07.210 --> 00:26:08.830
You another guest here?

00:26:10.770 --> 00:26:14.030
I'm sorry, my English.

00:26:16.310 --> 00:26:17.950
You're a choice for a vacation.

00:26:23.590 --> 00:26:30.970
Sometimes, to move beyond the past,
you must face it.

00:26:31.830 --> 00:26:35.090
Okay, some unexpected elder wisdom.

00:26:36.430 --> 00:26:39.438
For all guests of the Wolf's Lair Inn,
please join

00:26:39.480 --> 00:26:42.230
us at this time for a
delicious evening feast.

00:26:44.850 --> 00:26:45.910
Guess that's us.

00:26:48.270 --> 00:27:00.720
Tell me,

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:04.540
Miss Taylor, where do you come from?

00:27:05.900 --> 00:27:08.200
Oh, um, New York.

00:27:08.980 --> 00:27:11.940
I'm currently studying
world history at Columbia.

00:27:12.480 --> 00:27:16.320
It's a real passion of mine,
dissecting how our past impacts

00:27:16.362 --> 00:27:19.860
our present and how our
present will impact our future.

00:27:20.340 --> 00:27:25.129
Of particular interest to me right
now is these leftist regimes, working so

00:27:25.171 --> 00:27:30.000
hard to overthrow everything that has
always made America so great since its

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:30.360
founding.

00:27:31.120 --> 00:27:33.880
The old ways have always just felt so...

00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:35.480
superior.

00:27:36.220 --> 00:27:38.740
Well,
that's a strong viewpoint you have there.

00:27:39.420 --> 00:27:40.360
What about you guys?

00:27:40.680 --> 00:27:41.620
Where do you hail from?

00:27:45.240 --> 00:27:48.580
That's where we...

00:27:48.580 --> 00:27:49.500
hail from?

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:51.800
We're American.

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:53.140
Father, too.

00:27:53.940 --> 00:27:54.940
Mother is German.

00:27:54.940 --> 00:27:58.900
Ah, okay.

00:27:59.580 --> 00:28:02.320
Oh, and how'd you guys end up in Poland?

00:28:02.640 --> 00:28:03.340
Father's work.

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:06.100
He, too,
is quite passionate about history.

00:28:07.280 --> 00:28:08.880
Is that right?

00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:13.620
Well, I can't wait to meet him.

00:28:14.120 --> 00:28:15.200
Will you be joining us tonight?

00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:16.560
So here you smell.

00:28:19.560 --> 00:28:20.160
Vitami.

00:28:20.820 --> 00:28:21.420
Vitami.

00:28:22.240 --> 00:28:22.840
Vitami.

00:28:23.840 --> 00:28:24.440
Vitami.

00:28:24.440 --> 00:28:26.400
Apologies for our tardiness.

00:28:26.640 --> 00:28:28.020
It's been a long day.

00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:31.579
We're in the final stages
of a little something here at

00:28:31.621 --> 00:28:34.940
the lair to improve the state of things,
you could say.

00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:36.500
Ah, exciting.

00:28:37.780 --> 00:28:39.200
To put it lightly.

00:28:40.560 --> 00:28:42.440
But one must not, am I right?

00:28:43.320 --> 00:28:44.220
Where are my manners?

00:28:44.520 --> 00:28:44.760
Hello.

00:28:45.480 --> 00:28:46.220
I'm Wilhelm.

00:28:46.880 --> 00:28:48.460
My small friend here is Russell.

00:28:49.920 --> 00:28:51.800
It's so nice to meet you both.

00:28:51.800 --> 00:28:54.720
Wilhelm,
these are our guests for this evening.

00:28:55.220 --> 00:28:58.960
Miss Taylor and Mr. Emmanuel,
both solo travelers.

00:29:01.260 --> 00:29:02.320
Is that right?

00:29:09.860 --> 00:29:12.920
Well,
we are thrilled to have you both with us.

00:29:17.540 --> 00:29:21.020
Oh, Miss Taylor, you don't have
any sauerkraut on your plate.

00:29:21.360 --> 00:29:22.700
You really must try it.

00:29:22.940 --> 00:29:25.000
Um, no, it's all right.

00:29:25.100 --> 00:29:26.020
I'm not really...

00:29:26.020 --> 00:29:28.860
For one, for sauerkraut,
yes, that's what they all say.

00:29:29.780 --> 00:29:32.000
But this is Louise's specialty.

00:29:32.820 --> 00:29:33.760
You won't regret it.

00:29:34.420 --> 00:29:35.300
I insist.

00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:37.320
The best I ever had.

00:29:40.040 --> 00:29:43.020
Oh, well, in that case...

00:29:46.520 --> 00:29:48.320
Tell me, Helga, what did we miss?

00:29:48.740 --> 00:29:50.877
We were just having
a lovely conversation

00:29:50.919 --> 00:29:53.200
about Miss Taylor's
shared love for history.

00:29:53.840 --> 00:29:56.760
Ah,
do we have a fellow scholar in our midst?

00:29:57.300 --> 00:29:58.960
Uh, no, hardly a scholar.

00:30:00.310 --> 00:30:01.050
I can hold my own.

00:30:01.210 --> 00:30:01.570
Quick.

00:30:04.390 --> 00:30:05.470
What's this?

00:30:11.240 --> 00:30:12.060
That's the weapon.

00:30:14.600 --> 00:30:16.360
Very good, Miss Taylor.

00:30:16.740 --> 00:30:19.040
A symbol for slain warriors.

00:30:21.280 --> 00:30:23.900
And yet it would appear
you still walk among the living.

00:30:25.460 --> 00:30:28.520
But willing to perish at any time.

00:30:29.280 --> 00:30:30.540
Zy Kos.

00:30:31.659 --> 00:30:33.500
I must say I'm impressed.

00:30:34.340 --> 00:30:36.900
Where did you learn this history?

00:30:39.540 --> 00:30:43.860
Oh, I've just come across it
once or twice in my studies.

00:30:44.260 --> 00:30:49.640
I suppose some back in the States
do still teach appropriate curriculums.

00:30:50.140 --> 00:30:53.275
Helga and I found
our children's time at

00:30:53.317 --> 00:30:56.880
American schools to
be less than satisfactory.

00:30:57.260 --> 00:30:58.260
Is that a reason for the move?

00:31:02.680 --> 00:31:04.300
A contributing factor.

00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:05.420
Any other factors?

00:31:10.410 --> 00:31:13.710
You know what I think, Miss Taylor?

00:31:16.360 --> 00:31:20.200
I think you know exactly why we're here.

00:31:21.340 --> 00:31:26.380
Why we've come all this
way to Hare Wolf's Lair.

00:31:27.820 --> 00:31:42.090
It must have become fairly
obvious to you of history.

00:31:45.030 --> 00:31:46.890
Yeah, yeah, of course.

00:31:54.620 --> 00:31:56.520
Russell, we should get back to work.

00:31:56.800 --> 00:31:57.660
Apologies, children.

00:31:57.940 --> 00:31:58.880
We're just so close.

00:31:59.240 --> 00:32:00.200
How close?

00:32:01.240 --> 00:32:01.760
Tomorrow.

00:32:03.980 --> 00:32:05.580
What is it you said you were working on?

00:32:06.700 --> 00:32:07.360
I didn't.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:12.460
It's a pity you've all
still be here to find out.

00:32:16.240 --> 00:32:18.200
Yes, that reminds me.

00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:20.260
Um, I should be going to bed.

00:32:20.320 --> 00:32:21.960
I have to head out bright
and early tomorrow morning.

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:27.360
Alexis, you still haven't
tried your salt crumb, dear.

00:32:29.700 --> 00:32:30.260
Right.

00:32:30.900 --> 00:32:34.916
Look, you know, I was going to,
but then I thought to myself, how

00:32:34.958 --> 00:32:39.260
good could it be if Mr. Emanuel's
the only one at the table eating it?

00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:43.900
Nighty-night.

00:33:24.790 --> 00:33:27.130
I want to know who she is.

00:33:27.830 --> 00:33:29.210
Stay off the radio.

00:33:29.450 --> 00:33:31.930
If the Americans send another spy,
it might be close.

00:33:32.790 --> 00:33:33.530
Shut the gates.

00:33:34.070 --> 00:33:34.950
Set the blockades.

00:33:48.520 --> 00:33:49.760
Listen to us.

00:33:49.760 --> 00:33:51.920
Our parents,
they're not who they say they are.

00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:53.820
But they can't know that we said anything.

00:33:54.100 --> 00:33:57.180
I swear on my wife, Ms. Taylor,
you have to trust us.

00:33:57.260 --> 00:33:58.540
Then why would I trust you?

00:34:06.050 --> 00:34:07.170
Because we're telling the truth.

00:34:15.540 --> 00:34:19.339
I don't say ever just be
some fucking sauerkraut.

00:34:33.820 --> 00:34:36.053
We don't usually wake
our guests after dinner,

00:34:36.095 --> 00:34:38.320
say when my men
discovered your true identity.

00:34:38.700 --> 00:34:40.800
Well, I just had to say hello.

00:34:42.400 --> 00:34:45.280
I recognize that name immediately.

00:34:45.840 --> 00:34:50.260
Becky Hooper of the Hooper residence,
Lake Sinclair.

00:34:51.220 --> 00:34:56.320
That little girl who took out all my men
and stole my key all those years ago.

00:35:03.560 --> 00:35:05.120
And here you are.

00:35:07.450 --> 00:35:10.210
I should have known we'd
find ourselves meeting one day.

00:35:11.310 --> 00:35:14.870
History has shown time and time again.

00:35:17.110 --> 00:35:20.510
Take something from your enemy.

00:35:22.630 --> 00:35:26.030
Something that they love
more than anything in the world.

00:35:27.110 --> 00:35:29.170
And let them live to tell the tale.

00:35:30.230 --> 00:35:33.250
Like a cancer, they will grow.

00:35:35.210 --> 00:35:35.790
Why?

00:35:37.210 --> 00:35:38.090
Anger.

00:35:39.430 --> 00:35:42.110
The most powerful force of all.

00:35:45.790 --> 00:35:51.770
Five years ago, I instructed Dominic
to kill every person in that lake house.

00:35:53.090 --> 00:35:56.730
Outside of your father,
he proved to be incapable.

00:36:00.390 --> 00:36:04.070
I can assure you of this.

00:36:10.200 --> 00:36:14.160
Your father died for
an extraordinary cause.

00:36:17.560 --> 00:36:18.440
No!

00:36:28.400 --> 00:36:29.920
Please answer the question.

00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:34.220
How did you feel when
you watched your father die?

00:36:35.580 --> 00:36:37.060
I don't want to talk about this.

00:36:39.880 --> 00:36:40.520
Becky.

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:41.800
I love you, Becky.

00:36:42.300 --> 00:36:44.740
The most powerful force of all.

00:36:51.680 --> 00:36:54.980
If you're finished playing with your food,
darling.

00:36:55.980 --> 00:37:05.980
It appears it will be
your blood that brings

00:37:05.980 --> 00:37:08.100
about the next great chapter in history.

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:13.900
She's got spunk.

00:37:41.640 --> 00:37:42.950
Hold still, yeah?

00:37:43.730 --> 00:37:44.270
Nein.

00:38:26.500 --> 00:38:40.159
It works

00:38:40.159 --> 00:38:42.179
like that, the last vegetable.

00:39:45.140 --> 00:39:47.560
In today's session...

00:39:55.020 --> 00:39:55.920
This is Montana.

00:39:56.200 --> 00:39:57.560
There's another bunker underground.

00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:00.180
Often it pours beneath the layer.

00:40:00.500 --> 00:40:02.360
We destroyed all those
bunkers after the war.

00:40:02.720 --> 00:40:03.880
No, not this one.

00:40:04.340 --> 00:40:06.200
There's a lab inside,
but I can't access it.

00:40:06.500 --> 00:40:06.840
Jesus.

00:40:07.360 --> 00:40:08.000
There's more.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:10.740
I just sent over photos
of the inn's visitor log.

00:40:10.980 --> 00:40:11.640
Highlighted names.

00:40:12.220 --> 00:40:14.900
Cross-referenced those of any
missing persons over the last six months.

00:40:15.280 --> 00:40:15.900
Yeah, why?

00:40:16.640 --> 00:40:18.280
They've been killing guests.

00:40:19.360 --> 00:40:20.160
Solo travelers.

00:40:20.440 --> 00:40:23.420
Killing them, bleeding them,
and burning their bodies.

00:40:24.480 --> 00:40:26.900
You're storing the blood in these
temperature-controlled devices.

00:40:27.080 --> 00:40:27.560
It's precise.

00:40:27.700 --> 00:40:29.460
They must be using it for
some kind of experiment.

00:40:29.900 --> 00:40:30.040
Okay.

00:40:30.120 --> 00:40:31.020
Agent, your job is done.

00:40:31.120 --> 00:40:33.280
I need you to leave the lair
immediately and head to Langley.

00:40:33.400 --> 00:40:35.080
There will be a plane
waiting for you on the tarmac.

00:40:36.440 --> 00:40:38.400
I'm going to kill him, Montana.

00:40:38.640 --> 00:40:39.180
Whoa, what?

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:39.740
What?

00:40:40.100 --> 00:40:40.700
Sorry, what?

00:40:41.320 --> 00:40:44.589
I'm going to kill him,
his family, his

00:40:44.631 --> 00:40:48.280
men,
and anyone else that stands in my way.

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:50.520
Becky, listen to me.

00:40:50.600 --> 00:40:54.000
You were right before,
about things being bigger than me.

00:40:55.160 --> 00:40:57.420
Wilhelm Roos is responsible
for my dad's death.

00:40:57.680 --> 00:40:59.580
He's responsible for
everything that's happened

00:40:59.622 --> 00:41:01.440
to me since the day I
found that fucking key.

00:41:01.440 --> 00:41:04.560
If that's reason enough,
that's not why I have to do this.

00:41:05.060 --> 00:41:07.617
The thing is,
this man and his followers are

00:41:07.659 --> 00:41:10.660
capable of the pain they
will cause if they succeed.

00:41:13.710 --> 00:41:16.619
And if there's even
the slightest possibility

00:41:16.661 --> 00:41:19.290
of that happening,
we cannot protect you.

00:41:19.770 --> 00:41:21.290
We will contact the Polish authorities.

00:41:21.610 --> 00:41:22.990
They will initiate military action.

00:41:23.690 --> 00:41:26.190
You will become collateral damage.

00:41:26.450 --> 00:41:27.570
Do you understand that?

00:41:28.890 --> 00:41:30.650
Thank you for believing in me.

00:41:34.820 --> 00:41:35.900
Maybe Baker had a point.

00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:36.220
Becky?

00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:39.080
Maybe I was just a killing machine.

00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:44.060
But when it comes to killing Nazis,
maybe that ain't such a bad thing.

00:41:45.220 --> 00:41:46.300
We've got a problem.

00:41:46.980 --> 00:41:48.180
Charles,
I'm going to have to call you back.

00:41:49.620 --> 00:41:50.280
Who's coming?

00:41:50.440 --> 00:41:52.040
There's a lab underneath the Wolf's Lair.

00:41:52.480 --> 00:41:53.420
That's the heat signature.

